Requirement Minimum Requirement

Certified Driving Range Minimum 100 km.

Electric Energy Not exceeding 30 kWh / 100 km, measured in accordance with
Consumption the applicable test procedure prescribed under the Central Motor
Vehicles Rules, 1989.

Minimum Maximum Speed Minimum 50 km per hour.

Acceleration Minimum 1.04 m/s², measured at Gross Vehicle Weight (GVW).

Regenerative Braking Mandatory.

Vehicle Warranty Covered by a comprehensive manufacturer warranty, including
battery warranty, of not less than three (3) years.

Localisation Complies with the applicable localisation requirements prescribed
under these Guidelines.

6.3. The OEM shall demonstrate compliance with the applicable Phased Manufacturing
Programme (PMP) requirements adopted by the Government of NCT of Delhi for
Electric Four Wheeler Goods Carriers (N1 Category), based on the localisation
requirements prescribed under the FAME India Scheme Phase II, for the following
components:

6.3.1. HVAC;
6.3.2. Electric Compressor;
6.3.3. Power and Control Wiring Harness along with Connectors;
6.3.4. MCB / Circuit Breakers / Electric Safety Device;
6.3.5. AC Charging Inlet (Type 2);
6.3.6. DC Charging Inlet (CCS2 / CHAdeMO);
6.3.7. DC Charging Inlet (BEVC DC 001);
6.3.8. Traction Battery Pack;
6.3.9. Wheel Rim Integrated with Hub Motor, where applicable;
6.3.10. DC DC Converter;
6.3.11. Electronic Throttle;
6.3.12. Vehicle Control Unit (VCU);
6.3.13. On Board Charger;
6.3.14. Traction Motor;
6.3.15. Traction Motor Controller including Inverter;
6.3.16. Instrument Panel;
6.3.17. Lighting Components, including Headlamp, Tail Lamp, Indicators, Interior
Lamp and Flasher, as applicable; and
6.3.18. Body Panel.

